# CODEOWNERS — the access boundary INSIDE this single repo (ADR-0003).
#
# platform-config is the only repo FDEs touch (ADR-0001 D1). They freely open PRs against the
# tenant registry. But the security-sensitive paths below — the org foundation, the policy gate,
# the deploy engine, and CI — define the boundary that *contains* FDEs, so a change to them
# requires PLATFORM-TEAM review to merge.
#
# This file is INERT on its own. To make it real, the repo also needs:
#   1. Branch protection on `main` with "Require review from Code Owners" enabled.
#   2. A @aidaploco/platform-team GitHub team (write access) = the platform engineers.
#   3. A @aidaploco/fde-team GitHub team = the forward-deployed engineers.
# Replace those team slugs with your actual ones.

# Default: anything not matched below requires platform-team review.
*               @aidaploco/platform-team

# --- FDE-editable surface: the tenant registry is their whole job. ---
# Either an FDE or a platform engineer can approve a tenant change; the OPA policy gate
# (ADR-0001 D8) is the automated backstop on these PRs.
/tenants/       @aidaploco/fde-team @aidaploco/platform-team

# --- Platform-team-only (stated explicitly even though the default already covers them) ---
/bootstrap/     @aidaploco/platform-team
/policies/      @aidaploco/platform-team
/terraform/     @aidaploco/platform-team
/.github/       @aidaploco/platform-team
/docs/adr/      @aidaploco/platform-team
/VERSIONS.md    @aidaploco/platform-team
